# Output Style

## Code Formatting

- **2-space indentation** (no tabs)
- **Single quotes** for all strings
- **No semicolons** (omitted consistently)
- **No trailing commas** on the last item
- **Functional components only** — never use class components

## Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Route pages | `page.tsx` | Always `page.tsx` |
| Route layouts | `layout.tsx` | Always `layout.tsx` |
| Feature components | `PascalCase.tsx` | `CaseDialog.tsx`, `CaseTable.tsx` |
| Server actions (write) | `verbNounAction` | `createCaseAction`, `deleteCaseAction` |
| Server actions (read) | `getNoun` | `getCases`, `getTeamMembers` |
| Validation schemas | `nounSchema` | `caseSchema`, `inviteSchema` |
| Action files | `noun.ts` | `cases.ts`, `team.ts` |
| Validation files | `noun.ts` | Same as action file names |
| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` | `PLAN_SLUGS`, `MEMBER_ROLES` |
| Types | `PascalCase` | `ActionResult`, `AppStatus` |

## File Organization

- **Server actions** → `src/lib/actions/<module>.ts`
- **Validation schemas** → `src/lib/validations/<module>.ts`
- **Feature UI** → Co-located with route: `src/app/dashboard/<feature>/<Component>.tsx`
- **Shared UI** → `src/components/ui/` (shadcn primitives)
- **Layout components** → `src/components/layout/`
- **Admin components** → `src/app/(admin-panel)/admin/_components/`

## Error Messages

- **User-facing errors**: Always in Arabic
- **Internal logging**: Use `console.error()` with English context
- **Pattern**:
  ```typescript
  if (error) {
    console.error('Error creating case:', error)
    return { data: null, error: 'حدث خطأ أثناء إضافة القضية' }
  }
  ```

## Tailwind CSS

- Use utility classes inline (not extracted to CSS modules)
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- RTL: use `ms-*`/`me-*`, never `ml-*`/`mr-*`
- Colors via oklch design tokens (see `globals.css`)
- Admin panel: dark theme with zinc-950 backgrounds and amber accents
- Dashboard: light theme with gray-50 backgrounds

## Commits

- Use Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`
- Keep commits focused — one logical change per commit
- Explain schema-affecting changes in the commit body
